# From "Discovering Intuition" (Wave V - Exploring Focus 15, CD1-2). The
# trigger phrase is badly ASR-garbled in the source ("say to yourself plus no
# plus no and exhale") but the exact same "plus [verb] now" template appears
# clean twice in mission-15-creation-and-manifestation.gws's source tape
# ("plus create now... plus manifest now") -- "no" scans as a plausible
# mis-hearing of "know now" for an exercise about knowing. Reconstructed as
# "plus know now" on that basis, flagged here rather than left silently
# guessed at.

@segment  discovering-intuition
@title    Discovering Intuition
@levels   F12
@duration ~4m

say In Focus 12, let your consciousness expand even further. Deeper, well beyond your five physical senses.
pause 8
say Remember a time you just knew something was true, with no evidence for it. A hunch. A gut feeling. Maybe you even acted on it.
pause 8
say Recreate that memory now, as vividly as you can.
pause 10
say Now remember the feeling that came with that knowing. Let yourself feel it again, clearly.
pause 10
say Bring to mind other times you felt that same particular feeling. Recreate those too, as fully as you can.
pause 10
say Now let the images fade. Just keep the feeling.
pause 8
say That feeling is your own personal marker for intuition — a knowing you can trust.
pause 6
say This ability is natural to you. It's part of who you already are.
pause 6
say From now on, whenever you want to know something clearly: inhale, remember that feeling, and say in your mind — plus know now. Plus know now. Then exhale.
pause 8
say Do this, and your perception opens beyond the five senses. You'll know what you need to know, and what to do about it.
pause 8
say The more you practice this, the easier and more effective it becomes.
pause 6
